From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: clear the EOS flag when a buffer is queued

V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP marks the last queued source buffer with
MFC_BUF_FLAG_EOS. The flag is kept in the per-index buffer state and is
never cleared, so it is still set when the application queues the same
buffer index again after the drain. Decoding then stops (the context
enters the FINISHING state) every time that buffer is used, for example
after a seek in Kodi, which drains the decoder first.

The same applies to the destination buffers, which are marked with
MFC_BUF_FLAG_EOS when all frames are extracted.

Clear MFC_BUF_FLAG_EOS together with MFC_BUF_FLAG_USED when a buffer is
queued.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -1137,14 +1137,14 @@
 
 	if (vq->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE) {
 		mfc_buf = &ctx->src_bufs[vb->index];
-		mfc_buf->flags &= ~MFC_BUF_FLAG_USED;
+		mfc_buf->flags &= ~(MFC_BUF_FLAG_USED | MFC_BUF_FLAG_EOS);
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->irqlock, flags);
 		list_add_tail(&mfc_buf->list, &ctx->src_queue);
 		ctx->src_queue_cnt++;
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->irqlock, flags);
 	} else if (vq->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE) {
 		mfc_buf = &ctx->dst_bufs[vb->index];
-		mfc_buf->flags &= ~MFC_BUF_FLAG_USED;
+		mfc_buf->flags &= ~(MFC_BUF_FLAG_USED | MFC_BUF_FLAG_EOS);
 		/* Mark destination as available for use by MFC */
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->irqlock, flags);
 		set_bit(vb->index, &ctx->dec_dst_flag);
